course: dictionary
lesson: 6068
title: A mermaid, and a mermaid's purse
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mermaid is an imaginary sea creature with the head and body of a woman and the tail of a fish. Imaginary means it is made up, so you will not find one in the sea. Stories and myths are full of them, such as «The Little Mermaid» by Hans Christian Andersen.
explain: Use the words around a word to find its meaning. «The mermaid sang to the sailors from the rocks.» The words sea, sing and sailors tell you that the creature lives under the sea and sings to people on ships. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A sea creature, not a person with legs.
explain: Some words are part of a name, and then their usual meaning does not apply. «It is a mermaid's purse, an egg case that once held a baby shark or ray.» Here the purse is not a bag and the mermaid is not a creature with a fish tail. It is the name of an egg case.
fact: A mermaid is an imaginary sea creature with the head and body of a woman and the tail of a fish.
fact: A merman is the male version of a mermaid.
fact: In stories and myths, mermaids live under the sea, sing and sometimes lure sailors.
fact: Mermaids are not real, but sailors in the past may have mistaken manatees or dugongs for them.
fact: A «mermaid's purse» is the egg case of some sharks, skates and rays; its curly tendrils hold it to seaweed while the baby grows.
exercise: In «The mermaid sang to the sailors from the rocks.», what is the mermaid doing? | Selling fish at the harbour | Climbing the rocks on land | *Singing to the sailors | Sailing a ship
exercise: What is a merman? | *The male version of a mermaid | A sailor on a ship | A fish with a saw | A female mermaid
exercise: «It is a mermaid's purse, an egg case that once held a baby shark or ray.» What is a mermaid's purse? | A woman with a fish tail | A sailor's money bag | *An egg case of a shark or ray | A bag for sea shells
test: Mermaids are not real. Why might sailors in the past have thought they saw one? | Mermaids came up to the ships every day | They were looking at a shipwreck full of gold | *They may have mistaken manatees or dugongs for mermaids | Their maps showed where mermaids lived
test: «A mermaid's purse is the egg case of a catshark, skate or ray.» Which is true? | A mermaid's purse is a real mermaid's bag | A mermaid's purse is a fish with a woman's head | A mermaid's purse is a sailor's gift | *A mermaid's purse is an egg case that holds a baby fish
exam: Which is NOT true of a mermaid? | They are imaginary | They appear in stories and myths | *They are real animals found in the sea today | They have the tail of a fish
